Z||000000||fierosound||03-19-2001||07:57 PM||||This is a clear acrylic film that is applied to your headlights or PAINT surfaces to protect from rock chips.  Life expectancy of the product is approx. 5 years, after which it can be removed and a new film applied.  I've personally seen a similar product on a Jaguar and am considering it for my Fiero after the new paint goes on.  Has anyone seen or hear about these products and experiences??  I'd like to know.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.xpel.com/paint/applications.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xpel.com/paint/applications.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TigerFiero||03-19-2001||08:25 PM||||A friend had it put on his wifes miata.  I thought it looked stupid because you could see this line across the front where it ended.  Unless they could blend it in better, I wouldn't do it.<P>------------------<BR>TigerFiero<BR>86 Sport Coupe<BR>86 GT Fastback<BR>North Florida/South Georgia Fieros||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||03-20-2001||01:26 AM||||I agree.  On the Jag I saw, you could see the line too, but only when you're near it.  It's not noticeable further away.  On my Fiero, I'd take right up to the top of the facia to the hood/fender joints.||||reg||10
